A Custom Operation System Kernel

A simple, custom operation system kernel built from scratch in C and provided function in assembly. The project implements low-level basic OS functionalities and a software interrupt system call interface.

Features
	-Disk I/O: functions to read/write from and to disk storage.
	-Console I/O: functions to read user and print to screen.
	-System Calls: Int_21 used as a delegation method to call functions that provide the above 
			features.

Tools Used
	- Bash: automated script for testing/running simulator
	- NASM: assembly compilation
	- bcc/ld: compilation and linking
	- Emumaker86: simulator

How To:
	- Linux environment with nasm, bcc, as86, ld86, dd, and any text editor of choice.
	- Run the compileOS script. 
	- Select Hard Drive/CD C:
		>Navigate and select disk.img
		>Cylinders=63, Heads=255, Sectors=1000
		>Boot Disk C:
